  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-12T02:16:55.445Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Since the Avatar Dynamics update, I have noticed consistent and distracting linear stutter on my avatar hand movements and walking. It manifests in a few ways:\n- Avatar hands seem to be dropping many frames in a consistent manner. This is very visible if you keep your hands still in front of your face and move them along with your head movements. It is visible at all times regardless.\n- Walking has a consistent stutter. If you strafe very slowly, the world seems to be \"snapping\" to your new position rapidly.\nAfter asking friends about their experiences, it seems that this is consistent with Rift S headsets and not readily visible on the Quest 2 or Index.\nThis is on the latest Oculus Desktop version of VRChat.",
